/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
//
// String Table
//

STRINGTABLE 
BEGIN
    IDS_TOOLTIP_ICONTYPE    "How the load is shown in the tray: LED (brightness), Bar (Task Manager style), Clean bar, VU meter (segments), Graph (recent history) or Number."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_INVERT      "Show the 100% value minus the counter value, e.g. memory used from a counter that reports memory available."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COLORS      "Low, mid and high colour. Click to change. Used by all icon types (the LED uses the low colour)."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_THRESHOLDS  "Where the mid and the high colour start, in % of the scale (the 100% value, or the peak with the Peak and Decay scale)."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_AUTOSTART   "Start DiskLED when you log on to Windows. Adds a Startup entry for the current user, no admin rights needed."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_VALUEFORMAT "How to show the current value in the icon's tooltip. Use Bytes/s or Bits/s for counters measured in bytes per second, MBytes for counters measured in megabytes."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_UPDATE_FREQUENCY 
                            "How often to update the display (in milliseconds). Applies to all meters."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_SAVE        "Keep the settings. Changes are shown on the tray icons right away, but only kept after Save."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_REVERT      "Go back to the last saved settings."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_METERNAME   "A name for this meter, shown in its tooltip and in the list. Optional."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_SCALEMODE   "What corresponds to the full icon. Fixed: the 100% value. Peak: the highest of the last 16 values. Decay: a peak that slowly falls (halves in 30 s). Auto: the highest value DiskLED has seen, remembered in the INI file and falling very slowly (halves in a day). With Peak, Decay and Auto the 100% value is the minimum."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERSEL  "The meters. Each meter is one tray icon with its own data source, 100% value, format, scale, icon and warning. The settings below belong to the meter shown here."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_ADD_METER   "Add a meter (a tray icon). It starts as a copy of the meter shown, change its data source below."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_REMOVE_METER "Remove the meter that is shown, and its tray icon."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_ALERT       "Show a notification when the value stays above this percentage of the scale (the value that fills the icon) for this many seconds. 0% turns the warning off."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_DEFAULT_VALUES "Replace all meters by one default meter. Like every change, this can be undone with Revert until you Save."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_100PERCENT  "The counter value that is a full icon. You can type a plain number (the raw counter value) or a value with a unit, e.g. 350 Mbit/s or 50 MB/s for network and disk speeds. With the Peak, Decay and Auto scale this is only the minimum."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERPATH "From the selection above, build a performance counter path"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION "Description of the selected counter"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_OBJECTS     "Select a performance object"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERS    "Select a performance object's counter"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_INSTANCES   "Select a performance counter instance"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_USE_LINKSPEED 
                            "Use the speed of the network adapter as the 100% value (Fixed scale). This is the speed of the adapter, not of your internet connection, which is often lower."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_QUICKPICK   "Choose a common data source. DiskLED fills in the counter, the value format and the scale for you. You can change everything afterwards, or pick any counter with the lists below."
END

